        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2010",
        "question_text": "<p>The volume of a gas is 200 cm\u00b3 at 27\u00b0C. What will be its volume at 127\u00b0C if the pressure remains constant? (Assume ideal behavior)</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Using Charles's Law: $V_1/T_1 = V_2/T_2$. Convert temperatures to Kelvin: $T_1 = 27 + 273 = 300 K$, $T_2 = 127 + 273 = 400 K$. Then, $V_2 = (V_1 \\times T_2) / T_1 = (200 \\times 400) / 300 = 266.67$ cm\u00b3.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
            {
                "option_id": "66210",
